Resolve static interface and GVM dispatch cells against per-module data looked up once (NativeAOT).

Dispatch.ResolveDispatch runs on the first call through every dispatch cell, and again for each new
receiver type at a polymorphic call site. Each time it called RhGetModuleSection two or three times (a
linear scan of the module's ReadyToRun section table), re-initialized the module's native references
table through RhFindBlob (one more scan), and rebuilt the NativeReader and NativeArray header for the
cell-info section. None of that changes after the modules are loaded, so the cell regions, their decoded
info arrays and the native references are now computed once per module, on the first resolution, and
kept in a static array. Resolution itself is unchanged.

Nethermind stateless guest on ZisK (ziskemu 1.3.0): ResolveDispatch 2,035 -> ~1,310 steps per
resolution; 343 resolutions on block 26055159.
  block 26055159 steps 56,072,171 -> 55,823,836 (-0.44%)
  block 26112793 steps 131,086,840 -> 130,833,026 (-0.19%)
Outputs identical on 11 mainnet blocks.

